 4. 🕯️ D.C. marks 25 years since 9/11 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A fragment of the airplane that crashed into the Pentagon on 9/11. Photo: Smithsonian Institution The Smithsonian's National Museum of American History this week is highlighting about 40 objects tied to the World Trade Center, Pentagon and Flight 93 that are not currently on display, Axios D.C.'s Anna Spiegel reports. 

 The objects will be displayed on open tables rather than behind glass, for an unusually close look meant to "inspire respect and reflection." ⛑️ The Smithsonian's 9/11 collection has over 700 pieces, including plane and building fragments, first responders' gear, photographs and letters.

 The museum will also screen the documentary "9/11: Stories in Fragments." More events ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
